Day 1: Type System & Memory Architecture

Value types vs. reference types, stack vs. heap allocation, struct vs. class, ref struct, nullability mechanics (Nullable<T>, nullable reference types, compiler checks vs. runtime nulls).

Day 2: Object-Oriented Semantics & Modern Pattern Matching

Inheritance vs. composition, virtual/override vs. new, abstract classes vs. interfaces, records (record class vs. record struct), switch expressions, property and relational pattern matching.

Day 3: Generics, Collections & Delegates

Generic constraints (where T : class, new()), variance (in/out), collection internals (List<T>, Dictionary<TKey, TValue> hash collisions/growth factors), delegates, Func<T>, Action<T>, lambda expressions.

Day 4: Memory Optimization & Modern Types

Span<T>, ReadOnlySpan<T>, Memory<T>, string allocation overhead, ArrayPool<T>, in/out/ref parameters, unmanaged memory pointers (unsafe context overview).

Day 5: Garbage Collection & Resource Lifetime

Generations 0, 1, and 2, Large Object Heap (LOH), Ephemeral segment, GC triggers and compaction, IDisposable, IAsyncDisposable, the standard dispose pattern, SafeHandle.

ay 6: LINQ Architecture & Deferred Execution

IEnumerable<T> vs. IQueryable<T>, extension methods, deferred execution pitfalls (multiple enumeration, closure captures), custom LINQ query operators.

Day 7: Async/Await Mechanics & The State Machine

Task, ValueTask, TaskCompletionSource, how compiler transforms async/await into state machines, SynchronizationContext, thread pool task scheduling.

Day 8: Advanced Concurrency & Coordination

CancellationToken propagation, SemaphoreSlim, Channel<T> for producer-consumer workloads, lock-free primitives (Interlocked), concurrent collections (ConcurrentDictionary<TKey, TValue>).

Day 9: Reflection, Attributes & Source Generators

Type inspection via System.Reflection, custom attributes, compile-time Roslyn Source Generators vs. runtime reflection overhead, emit & dynamic dispatch.

Day 10: Serialization & Core CLI Tooling

System.Text.Json (custom converters, contract resolvers, source-generation mode), .csproj property inspection, multi-targeting, CLI profiling with dotnet-dump, dotnet-trace.

Day 11: Relational Modeling & Normalization

1NF to BCNF trade-offs, constraints (foreign keys, check, unique), surrogate vs. natural keys, schema versioning strategies.

Day 12: Indexing Internals & B-Tree Structures

Clustered vs. non-clustered indexes, index fragmentation, fill factor, composite index column ordering, covered queries (INCLUDE).

Day 13: Execution Plans & Query Tuning

Reading graphical/XML execution plans: Index Seek vs. Index Scan, Hash Match, Nested Loops, Sort spills to tempdb, identifying parameter sniffing.

Day 14: Transactions, Concurrency & Locking

ACID properties, isolation levels (Read Committed, Repeatable Read, Serializable, Snapshot), lock types (shared, exclusive, update), deadlocks and graph analysis.

Day 15: Advanced SQL & ORM Integration Patterns

Window functions (ROW_NUMBER, RANK, LEAD/LAG), CTEs, stored procedures vs. dynamic SQL, mapping data access through Entity Framework Core (tracking vs. no-tracking, batching) and micro-ORMs like Dapper.

